@ping1jing2 @iforgetmyname @whybeyoung @ssshinigami @e-martirosian @Kangyan-Zhou @Fridge003 @ranjiewen @ClownBin @huangxiaojun15

Following up on this community contribution, open since October 13. Current head `cdc614e` passed the registered single-A3 GPT-OSS-20B regression: short/long prompts of 80/282 tokens, 8 generated tokens each, 2 HTTP subcases passed, 0 skips. The test used the isolated SwiGLU UB-capacity fix documented in the PR.

Please confirm named owners for (1) FIA dispatch/layout and test review, (2) a maintained package containing an equivalent SwiGLU fix and the pinned BF16 checkpoint cache, and (3) `run-ci` authorization and rerunning `base-b-test-1-npu-a3` with that package. My October 26 dependency update is still awaiting a response. The earlier kernel contributions remain withdrawn; this request is for the dependency needed by the open SGLang regression. Please provide the package/version, cache owner and expected review/CI date so this PR can proceed to merge. Thank you.

